    "explanation": "The text explicitly frames Senator Richard Blumenthal as accusing Wilbur Ross of being a 'Deceiver'. Blumenthal states that Ross 'deceived the public' and claims the Paradise Papers 'twisted the story,' while simultaneously asserting Ross misled lawmakers who confirmed his appointment. This positions Ross within the narrative function of a Deceiver (one who twists truth/misinformation) according to the accuser's framing, which is central to the text's conflict."
  },
