{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "President Trump and the sheriffs are framed as Guardians of law enforcement authority. Trump explicitly defends the power of law enforcement agencies to seize assets, stating there is 'no reason' to curb them, positioning himself as a protector of police powers against legislative interference. The sheriffs are portrayed as allies in this protective stance, reporting pressure to ease practices that they view as necessary for disrupting crime."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "While lawmakers introducing bills to reform forfeiture could theoretically be seen as Rebels or Underdogs challenging the status quo, the text primarily frames their efforts as obstacles to be overcome by the President and law enforcement. The narrative focus is on the conflict between executive/police power and legislative reform, but the text does not sufficiently elevate the lawmakers to the role of altruistic catalysts driving systemic change; rather, they are depicted as critics whose concerns are dismissed or threatened against by the primary actors."
