  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "China's Foreign Minister Wang Yi is framed as a Peacemaker and Guardian of stability. He advocates for 'negotiations' as the 'only way out,' urges parties to play a 'constructive role in easing tensions,' and emphasizes that there is 'still hope for peace.' His actions are positioned as efforts to maintain social cohesion and safety through diplomacy and mediation rather than conflict."
